WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.770
Find a position that feels stable enough for the next few minutes.

2
00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:09.570
Let the hands rest, soften your gaze, or close your eyes if that is comfortable.

3
00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:14.760
Notice two or three points where the body is supported.

4
00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:20.050
You can move, open your eyes, or stop whenever you choose.

5
00:00:32.822 --> 00:00:35.042
Begin with the breath as it already is.

6
00:00:36.742 --> 00:00:38.602
There is no need to make it slower or deeper.

7
00:00:40.302 --> 00:00:44.022
Feel one complete inhale and one complete exhale.

8
00:00:45.722 --> 00:00:48.952
Choose the place where the movement is easiest to recognize.

9
00:01:04.917 --> 00:01:08.617
We will use a light count to give attention a simple task.

10
00:01:10.317 --> 00:01:13.957
As the next exhale ends, silently say one.

11
00:01:15.657 --> 00:01:17.777
With the following exhale, say two.

12
00:01:19.477 --> 00:01:22.277
Continue until five, then begin again at one.

13
00:01:54.207 --> 00:01:56.067
The count is not a test of memory.

14
00:01:57.767 --> 00:02:04.217
If you lose the number, discover that you have reached eight, or forget that you were counting, notice what happened without correcting the past.

15
00:02:05.917 --> 00:02:07.517
The next exhale can be one.

16
00:02:34.126 --> 00:02:35.436
Continue from one to five.

17
00:02:37.136 --> 00:02:40.076
Let each number arrive near the end of the exhale.

18
00:02:41.776 --> 00:02:44.366
Leave the inhale uncounted and unhurried.

19
00:02:46.066 --> 00:02:49.346
One breath, one quiet number, then space for the next breath.

20
00:03:31.919 --> 00:03:33.519
Check for unnecessary effort.

21
00:03:35.219 --> 00:03:39.559
Counting does not require a tight forehead, a held jaw, or a controlled breath.

22
00:03:41.259 --> 00:03:43.509
Let the face and hands receive a little more room.

23
00:03:45.209 --> 00:03:49.619
Keep only enough effort to recognize the exhale and remember the next number.

24
00:04:16.228 --> 00:04:17.188
Begin another round.

25
00:04:18.888 --> 00:04:19.478
One.

26
00:04:21.178 --> 00:04:21.468
Two.

27
00:04:23.168 --> 00:04:23.628
Three.

28
00:04:25.328 --> 00:04:25.708
Four.

29
00:04:27.408 --> 00:04:27.878
Five.

30
00:04:29.578 --> 00:04:33.908
If the breathing rhythm changes, allow the counting rhythm to change with it.

31
00:04:35.608 --> 00:04:37.208
No breath has to wait for the number.

32
00:05:25.103 --> 00:05:27.403
Now notice where attention tends to go.

33
00:05:29.103 --> 00:05:34.303
Perhaps into a plan, a sound, an image, or a judgment about the practice.

34
00:05:36.003 --> 00:05:37.883
The content does not need to be removed.

35
00:05:39.583 --> 00:05:44.163
Recognize thinking, feel one point of support, and let the next exhale be one.

36
00:06:16.093 --> 00:06:17.793
For a while, count to ten instead.

37
00:06:19.493 --> 00:06:21.083
Use the same gentle approach.

38
00:06:22.783 --> 00:06:26.033
If ten creates strain or confusion, return to five.

39
00:06:27.733 --> 00:06:30.003
The useful part is not reaching the last number.

40
00:06:31.703 --> 00:06:34.403
It is recognizing the moment of return.

41
00:07:38.263 --> 00:07:39.353
Release the count.

42
00:07:41.053 --> 00:07:44.413
Let two or three breaths pass without numbers.

43
00:07:46.113 --> 00:07:49.453
Notice whether the breath feels different when the small task is gone.

44
00:07:51.153 --> 00:07:52.833
There is no preferred result.

45
00:08:14.120 --> 00:08:18.390
Bring the count back for one final round from one to five.

46
00:08:20.090 --> 00:08:26.220
See if the numbers can be quieter now, almost like markers placed beside the breath rather than instructions given to it.

47
00:09:08.793 --> 00:09:10.163
Let the final number go.

48
00:09:11.863 --> 00:09:14.763
Feel the body as a whole, supported and breathing.

49
00:09:16.463 --> 00:09:19.363
Include sounds in the room without following them.

50
00:09:21.063 --> 00:09:23.333
Include thoughts without needing to finish them.

51
00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:46.480
Notice the next movement before you make it.

52
00:09:48.180 --> 00:09:50.790
Let the eyes open or focus more clearly.

53
00:09:52.490 --> 00:09:54.840
Counting offered a path back, not a score.

54
00:09:56.540 --> 00:10:00.000
You can begin with one whenever you need a simple place to return.
